WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.058
Begin with the complete memory budget.

00:00:03.058 --> 00:00:08.562
The quantized weights must fit alongside runtime buffers and the key-value cache.

00:00:08.562 --> 00:00:13.658
The cache grows with context length, active sequences, and model architecture.

00:00:13.658 --> 00:00:16.308
Batch settings add temporary pressure.

00:00:16.308 --> 00:00:22.220
Leave headroom instead of selecting a file whose size nearly equals available VRAM.

00:00:22.220 --> 00:00:27.316
Full GPU offload is often fastest when supported and memory allows.

00:00:27.316 --> 00:00:38.936
Partial offload places some layers on the GPU and leaves the rest on the CPU, which can enable a larger model but increase transfer and CPU work.

00:00:38.936 --> 00:00:46.070
CPU-only inference remains practical for smaller quantized models when system RAM and memory bandwidth are sufficient.

00:00:46.070 --> 00:00:54.428
Unified-memory systems share capacity between CPU and GPU, so the model competes with the operating system and other applications.

00:00:54.428 --> 00:00:59.117
Context can change a successful startup into an allocation failure.

00:00:59.117 --> 00:01:03.806
Test the configured maximum as well as a normal prompt.

00:01:03.806 --> 00:01:09.717
Measure time to first token, prompt-processing speed, generation speed, VRAM, RAM, and stability.

00:01:09.717 --> 00:01:19.298
A model that barely fits may run slowly, prevent other applications from using the GPU, or fail when a long document arrives.

00:01:19.298 --> 00:01:22.356
Optimize for the actual service envelope.

00:01:22.356 --> 00:01:32.752
A smaller or slightly more compressed model that remains fully accelerated with context headroom may outperform a higher-precision version that spills into system memory.

00:01:32.752 --> 00:01:39.480
Conversely, if both fit comfortably, higher precision may offer better quality with little operational cost.

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:44.984
Hardware fit determines which comparison is meaningful; measurements determine which option wins.
